      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I second this. I already expressed my opinion on the recent UI changes inside of VRChat being BAD, and the new desktop HUD just follows suite. Notifications don't follow the placement inside of VR, they shouldn't be on top of the screen. You are creating dissociation between the two platforms (PCVR and Desktop). It's counterintuitive, because on the rare occasion I go on desktop I expect the SAME experience as I get while in VR. The elements are displaced and my eyes land where my mic indicator should be - surprise - it's not there. I am tired of you guys breaking the familiar experience and messing with our muscle memory. The new design is: ugly, cluttered, counterintuitive, and everything is moved to the corners of the display where it's hard to see. Moreover, I like using the \"experimental\" outline only icon for my mic indicator to get better immersion - that is gone now too. Please, stop introducing pointless changes that don't work for the sake of making changes.\n\nBig thumb down from me.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
